    "bonus_track": true,
    "based_on": "03 Noncommutative Horizon",
    "author": "Claude (Sonnet 5) -- creative side-experiment, not part of Gemini's main 8-track run",
    "concept": "Two symmetry operators applied in either order land somewhere different. The same four-note motif is played by two waveguide-plucked string voices, one forward, one reversed, panned apart, never resolving into unison -- the discrepancy between orders made audible. G harmonic minor's raised 7th, and a borrowed natural 9 in the final chord's sharp-5, are the 'wrong notes' that keep the symmetry from ever quite closing."
